## Layering (dbt best practice)

```text
googlesheets.* / kobotoolbox.*
        │
        ▼  staging (views)
stg_googlesheets__* / stg_kobotoolbox__* / stg_processed__*
        │
        ▼  intermediate
int_mentee_database (current ∪ legacy)
int_emonc_*  |  int_newborn_*
        │
        ▼  marts
mart_emonc_curriculum_completion
mart_individual_mentee_emonc_curriculum_progress
mart_newborn_curriculum_completion
        │
        ▼  metrics
metric_emonc_*_by_cycle
metric_*_progress_count / metric_average_score_progress
metric_newborn_*_by_cycle
```

| Layer | Materialization | Rule |
|-------|-----------------|------|
| staging | view | No business filters beyond null/trim; keep raw grain |
| intermediate | table | One clear job per model; reusable across marts |
| marts | table | Stable grain + column names for Power BI |
| metrics | table | Aggregations / rates only — never re-implement mart logic |

## Mart 1: cohort-aware EmONC curriculum completion

Port of `mentee_curriculum_completion_progress`.

- **Grain:** one row per `(mentee_id, cycle_id)`, including empty mentee×cycle rows
- **Mentee spine:** EmONC / both from mentee sheets, plus fact-only mentees
- **Skill avg:** AVG of per-skill MAX(average_score) within mentee×cycle
- **Skill assessments:** exclude Partograph
- **Cohort 1:** 11 CME, 5 drills, 18 skill demo, 18 return demo, 1 labor, 18 skill eval
- **Cohort 2+:** 13 CME, 5 drills, 20 skill demo, 20 return demo, 1 labor, 20 skill eval
- **date_completed:** first date when ALL six thresholds met; else NULL

| dbt model | Role |
|-----------|------|
| `int_emonc_cohorts` | cohort windows + requirements |
| `int_emonc_mentees` / `int_emonc_mentee_cycles` | spine × cycles |
| `int_emonc_curriculum_activity_progress` | CME / drills / demos / labor |
| `int_emonc_skill_evaluation_progress` | skill evals |
| `mart_emonc_curriculum_completion` | BI fact |
| `mart_individual_mentee_emonc_curriculum_progress` | 2026-activated mentee activity counts |
| `metric_emonc_*_coverage_by_cycle` | component coverage |

## Mart 1b: individual EmONC mentee progress (calendar year)

Port of Individual Mentee Curriculum Completion Progress Tracker.

- **Grain:** one row per `mentee_id` (not cohort-aware)
- **Spine:** EmONC / both with `toYear(date_activated) = emonc_progress_year` (default 2026)
- **Counts:** distinct topics for CME / drills / skill demos / return demos / labor monitoring
  submitted in the progress year; distinct skill evaluations (Partograph excluded) + avg score
- **Labor topics:** `Partograph*` prefix or `Labor_Monitoring` / `Labor Monitoring`
- **Includes** mentees with zero activity (LEFT JOIN counts)

| dbt model | Role |
|-----------|------|
| `mart_individual_mentee_emonc_curriculum_progress` | BI fact for annual individual progress |
| `metric_cme_progress_count` | sum/avg of `cme_count` by progress year |
| `metric_drill_progress_count` | sum/avg of `drill_count` |
| `metric_skill_demos_progress_count` | sum/avg of `skill_demos_count` |
| `metric_return_demos_progress_count` | sum/avg of `return_demos_count` |
| `metric_skill_eval_progress_count` | sum/avg of `skill_eval_count` |
| `metric_average_score_progress` | avg of `average_score` |
| `metric_labor_monitoring_progress_count` | sum/avg of `labor_monitoring_count` |
| `metric_individual_mentee_emonc_curriculum_progress` | AVERAGEX of capped progress ratio (DAX mirror) |

Caps for the composite metric (Cohort 2+ defaults): CME 13, drills 5, skill demos 20,
return demos 20, skill eval 20, avg-score flag 1 (`average_score >= 0.85`), labor 1
→ denominator **80**.

## Mart 2: cohort-aware newborn curriculum completion

Port of `newborn_curriculum_completion_progress`.

- **Grain:** one row per `(mentee_id, cycle_id)`, including empty mentee×cycle rows
- **Mentee spine:** newborn curriculum / both from `int_mentee_database`, plus fact-only
- **Requirements (all cohorts):** 19 CME, 7 drills, 20 practicum essential / 22 comprehensive,
  5 skill demo, 12 videos, 2 roleplay, 9 case scenarios, 7 group discussions
- **Practicum:** essential → activity `practicums` + `essential_newborn_care`;
  comprehensive → `Practicums` + `comprehensive_newborn_care` (prefer essential when both);
  staging lowercases activity — program selects the track
- **NNR:** first attempt = baseline, last attempt = endline within cycle;
  complete when both present and endline ≥ 0.85
- **date_completed:** first date when ALL nine thresholds met; else NULL
- **Windows:** inclusive on both ends

